From 85f4c53291ac84e2d11cf636748d5caf68e7f74a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode <user@example.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:12:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/29] turnip/a5xx: add depth/stencil attachment support

Emit the a5xx depth/stencil state at draw time: RB_DEPTH_BUFFER_INFO/
BASE/PITCH/ARRAY_PITCH, GRAS_SU_DEPTH_BUFFER_INFO, RB_STENCIL_INFO with
optional separate stencil, RB_DEPTH_CNTL from the dynamic depth state,
the depth-plane controls and the stencil control/refmask registers.
LRZ is disabled (no LRZ buffer is allocated), and the depth CCU is
invalidated before the draw and flushed afterwards.

Depth/stencil is the one image class that must stay tiled: the hardware
does not support linear D/S and RB_DEPTH_BUFFER_INFO has no tile-mode
field. Keep the fdl6 tiled layout for it, just disable UBWC.

Render-pass clears for D/S also use the CP_MEM_WRITE fill. D16, D24S8,
D32 and D32S8 (separate stencil) are supported. D24S8 has depth and
stencil in one dword, so a single-aspect clear is only done when the
other aspect is DONT_CARE. Note: use double for the 24-bit packing, a
float cannot represent 16777215.5 and rounds up into the stencil byte.

Tests: tu5_depth_test (D32) and 'tu5_depth_test d24s8' draw a full-screen
red triangle at z=0.75, a smaller blue one at z=0.25 and a full-screen
green one at z=0.9 which must be rejected. Both PASS with 3584 red +
512 blue pixels, no green. The whole 16-test suite still PASSes.
